9 completed trips, a rate of 0.008, below the thresholds of 4 and 0.08) and that POL-NS-09(c) and (d) are not engaged (rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and neither profile shows a counterparty dispute in 90 days) is accepted.\n\nNo escalation. This is not a case of two admissible artifacts in unresolvable conflict: the trip record's wait timer and the GPS trace's in-geofence run are reconciled by POL-NS-01(c) and POL-NS-05, which say from which fix the clock runs. No artifact carrying the deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08: the GPS trace has 100.0% coverage, 80 fixes, no gaps longer than 120 seconds and no clock skew over 90 seconds, the chat log's single message matches trip_record.chat_message_count, and the fare line reconciles. The traffic advisory is MISSING (weight 0.0) and carries nothing; it changes nothing here, because the trace contains a single in-geofence interval, so no accumulation under POL-NS-06(i) was possible in any event. The two advocate claims that cite that MISSING advisory without naming its MISSING_ARTIFACT issue code are discarded in the audit record, as POL-GEN-02(1) requires, and nothing in this ruling rests on that artifact.\n\nConfidence is 0.92. The 150-second dwell is carried by EV-GPS-02750 and the 180-second requirement and cancellation time by EV-TRIP-02750, both at weight 1.0, so the cap is 1.0. The monetary effect is SGD 4.50, below the SGD 8.00 automatic execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so the refund executes on issue. Both parties may appeal this provisional ruling once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
